# Panel 186 R7, lane land186, 2026-10-02: a group's record over a C union is
# built naming exactly one member of each union, an anonymous struct's fields
# counting as one, and every field outside them (spec § 13). What a
# construction leaves out is judged by `build`, from the header's layout, at
# the construction (`selfhost/emit/layout_sites.hero`).
#
# The natural program the sitting's second blind reading described: the
# record names both arms, the construction names `f`, and `p == q` is refused
# on the record, because an `f32` arm is not compared bit for bit (R3). The
# construction itself is legal; only the comparison is told.

extern "ffi-a-construction.h"
    record SA  #~ ffi_union_field
        kind: i32
        i: i32
        f: f32
        x: i32
    function make_sa() -> SA
    function sa_f(s: SA) -> f32

function main()
    b = SA(kind: 2, f: 1.5, x: 4)
    print(sa_f(b))
    p = make_sa()
    q = make_sa()
    print(p == q)
